    "body": "**Hub, 1100MX at 2500 rpm (contributor):** `1100mx_s2500.nc` ran clean on the 1100MX SIM in **both LO and HI** (0:33 each). So Hub does not model the belt: the RPM DRO shows the commanded 2500 either way, and cycle time doesn't depend on rpm. The note's basis is UM10586 §8.5.1/8.5.3 (1100MX: Low 70-2000 rpm, High 250-10,000 rpm), so 2500 rpm needs the high belt on a real machine. The simulator can't confirm or refute that, so this note stays manual-backed, not Hub-verified.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
