    "body": "**GUI tap check (contributor):** a TAP-M6 Drill op on a Ø6 hole, posted with the Tormach PathPilot post:\n- **1100MX:** posted `G98` / `G84 X0 Y0 Z-0.1681 R0 F23.62` / `G80`. F is 600 rpm × 1.0 mm = 23.62 in/min, and there is no P word.\n- **770M:** refused, and no file was written. The UI shows the reason only on the status line, which hover text overwrites. That is pre-existing UI behaviour, not part of this PR.\n\nPinned on the Post button's own path by `a_tap_job_posts_on_the_1100mx_and_is_refused_on_the_770m` (c61da8e).\n\n**Found along the way (pre-existing, not this PR):** the material-sim gouge check sweeps a tap as a full-diameter cylinder. A tap on a hole modelled at the tap-drill size (Ø4–5 mm for M6) is refused as a gouge, so the hole had to be modelled at Ø6.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
