    "body": "**Hub, 1100MX SIM, tap (contributor):** `program.nc` loads, and PathPilot accepts the `G84` (line 14) with T2, 600 rpm and F23.6. The simulator then stops with \"Spindle reversal exceeded maximum overshoot in rigid tapping cycle\". That is the same simulator limit recorded on #162: every rigid tap in Hub stops there, at any rpm, because the simulated spindle doesn't run. The real 770MX ran the same G84 shape clean. So the 1100MX tap is Hub-verified up to the cycle start; it is not cut-verified (no 1100MX on hand).",
